{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1879018,
  "courseSlug": "nodejs-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "NodeJS - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342137",
      "title": "Understanding Generics",
      "lectureOrder": 503,
      "videoOrder": 445,
      "sourceHash": "32388a90e2a5cf399ff6ff00ab12d1ef8c092d4c45e6c158883e9d8191822b01",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 3.63,
          "en": "Now, last, but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.63,
          "end": 7.98,
          "en": "to sum up this basics refresher, let's talk about generics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.98,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "Generics are a feature that can look very confusing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 14.03,
          "en": "at first, but it makes a lot of sense.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.03,
          "end": 17.9,
          "en": "Actually, in our code here, we already have a generic type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.9,
          "end": 20.09,
          "en": "our two array types here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.09,
          "end": 22.29,
          "en": "A generic type simply is a type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.29,
          "end": 24.83,
          "en": "that interacts with another type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.83,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "and an array is a great example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 29.8,
          "en": "An array is a type on its own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.8,
          "end": 32.88,
          "en": "It's a list of data, that's the core type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.88,
          "end": 35.15,
          "en": "but it interacts with another type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.15,
          "end": 37.86,
          "en": "the type of data inside of the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.86,
          "end": 41.03,
          "en": "So, you could say that the array is the outer type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.03,
          "end": 43.5,
          "en": "but then you have all the elements in the array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 45.4,
          "en": "as an inner type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.4,
          "end": 48.7,
          "en": "And this here, this way of defining an array type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.7,
          "end": 51.46,
          "en": "is actually just a shortcut in TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.46,
          "end": 53.33,
          "en": "The longer form would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.33,
          "end": 56.77,
          "en": "that we set numResults to type Array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.77,
          "end": 59.46,
          "en": "but now array is a so-called generic type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 63.85,
          "en": "and you have to define the wrapped, the inner type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.85,
          "end": 67.39,
          "en": "in this case, the value types of the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.39,
          "end": 69.49,
          "en": "inside of the array, and you do so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.49,
          "end": 71.48,
          "en": "by adding angle brackets here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.48,
          "end": 74.09,
          "en": "the smaller than and the greater than sign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.09,
          "end": 77.23,
          "en": "and, between that, the generic type of array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.23,
          "end": 79.44,
          "en": "So, in this case, number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.44,
          "end": 83.57,
          "en": "And this says that numResults is an array full of numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.57,
          "end": 87.53,
          "en": "Now, what the thing between angle brackets refers to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.53,
          "end": 90.58,
          "en": "depends on the generic type you are working with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.58,
          "end": 94.33,
          "en": "Another example for a generic type would be a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.33,
          "end": 97.551,
          "en": "Now, for that, we can create a new promise down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.551,
          "end": 100.28999999999999,
          "en": "myPromise, by calling new Promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.28999999999999,
          "end": 102.59,
          "en": "And, by default, this code won't work here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.59,
          "end": 106.22999999999999,
          "en": "because we need to add a library to tsconfig",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.22999999999999,
          "end": 109.95,
          "en": "to, basically, tell tsconfig which kind of features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.95,
          "end": 111.56,
          "en": "we wanna support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.56,
          "end": 114.78999999999999,
          "en": "And, for example, by default here, because of this target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.58,
          "en": "it's configured to compile the TypeScript code down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.58,
          "end": 121,
          "en": "to es5 JavaScript code, which is quite old.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121,
          "end": 125.82,
          "en": "If we pick es6 here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.7,
          "end": 129.01,
          "en": "now this will work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.01,
          "end": 131.63,
          "en": "We still get an error, but now it's a different error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.63,
          "end": 134.6,
          "en": "So, we just have to ensure that we're telling TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.6,
          "end": 136.86,
          "en": "that we're working with a JavaScript version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.86,
          "end": 138.44,
          "en": "that supports promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.44,
          "end": 141.15,
          "en": "Because promise, of course, is not a TypeScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.15,
          "end": 143.19,
          "en": "it can't be compiled to something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.19,
          "end": 144.92000000000002,
          "en": "that works in older JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.92000000000002,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "Instead, we need to tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "that we wanna compile to JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 150.43,
          "en": "which natively supports promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 150.43,
          "end": 154.67000000000002,
          "en": "And that's what we just did by changing the target to es6.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.67000000000002,
          "end": 157.68,
          "en": "With that, we can define our promise here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.68,
          "end": 162.293,
          "en": "And a promise gets an argument which is a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.53,
          "end": 165.99,
          "en": "and that function itself gets two arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.99,
          "end": 168.35,
          "en": "a resolve and a reject function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.35,
          "end": 171.81,
          "en": "and, inside of the promise when we define it on our own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.81,
          "end": 175.86,
          "en": "we can, for example, set a timeout to execute some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.86,
          "end": 179.64,
          "en": "after a second, and after that second we resolve the promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.64,
          "end": 181.593,
          "en": "with, It worked!",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.81,
          "end": 185.24,
          "en": "And then, we can use our own promise here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.67,
          "end": 191.67,
          "en": "to listen to the result, and console.log it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.05,
          "end": 195.26,
          "en": "And we could also add catch to react to the rejection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.26,
          "end": 196.32,
          "en": "of the promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.32,
          "end": 198.29,
          "en": "And now, let's compile this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 198.29,
          "end": 200.27,
          "en": "By the way, now with a config file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.27,
          "end": 202.9,
          "en": "don't select the file manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.9,
          "end": 205.32999999999998,
          "en": "otherwise the config file won't be taken into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.32999999999998,
          "end": 206.24,
          "en": "by the compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.24,
          "end": 208.09,
          "en": "It is taken into account by the IDE,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 208.09,
          "end": 209.77,
          "en": "but not by the compiler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 209.77,
          "end": 213.61,
          "en": "Instead, just press tsc like this, enter tsc like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 213.61,
          "end": 216.5,
          "en": "and it will compile all TypeScript files in the folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 216.5,
          "end": 219.01,
          "en": "And now, it compiled this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 219.01,
          "end": 223.86,
          "en": "And if we now reload, you see, It worked, after one second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 223.86,
          "end": 226.73,
          "en": "But now, why is the promise a generic type?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 226.73,
          "end": 229.42000000000002,
          "en": "Because it eventually resolves to a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 229.42000000000002,
          "end": 231.63,
          "en": "and the value it resolves to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 231.63,
          "end": 234.17000000000002,
          "en": "that's the generic type for the promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.17000000000002,
          "end": 237.24,
          "en": "For the array, it was the value stored in the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.24,
          "end": 240.38,
          "en": "For the promise, it's the value the promise resolves to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 240.38,
          "end": 242.93,
          "en": "And, for example, here it resolves to a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.93,
          "end": 246.7,
          "en": "and, hence, we should be able to call split here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 246.7,
          "end": 251.7,
          "en": "for example, and split on the w.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 251.85,
          "end": 252.99,
          "en": "But this does not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 252.99,
          "end": 255.06,
          "en": "because TypeScript does not understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.06,
          "end": 256.52,
          "en": "that this is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 256.52,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "It does not know the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 262.1,
          "en": "Well, by adding angle brackets after Promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 262.1,
          "end": 265.81,
          "en": "we can set the type to which promise will resolve to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.81,
          "end": 267.24,
          "en": "to a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.24,
          "end": 270.89,
          "en": "Now, you can't set angle brackets on every built-in object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.89,
          "end": 273.23,
          "en": "It needs to be an object that supports this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.23,
          "end": 276.54,
          "en": "but the promise object, the promise constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 276.54,
          "end": 280.51,
          "en": "does support generic types because you can set the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 280.51,
          "end": 282.8,
          "en": "the promise will eventually resolve to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 282.8,
          "end": 286.1,
          "en": "And now, you see that split down there works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 286.1,
          "end": 289.03,
          "en": "and if I recompile this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.03,
          "end": 292.64,
          "en": "we see an array, it orked!, because of split.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 292.64,
          "end": 297.18,
          "en": "So, generic types can be tricky the first time you see them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 297.18,
          "end": 298.92,
          "en": "but they make a lot of sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 298.92,
          "end": 302.04,
          "en": "and they give you extra type safety",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 302.04,
          "end": 304.53,
          "en": "when working with more complex types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 304.53,
          "end": 307.483,
          "en": "or types that are simply connected to each other.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
